[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186190996 :answer-field/choices 17592186190997] [:db/retract 17592186190996 :answer-field/choices 17592186190998] [:db/retract 17592186190996 :answer-field/choices 17592186190999] [:db/retract 17592186190996 :answer-field/choices 17592186191000] [:db/retract 17592186190996 :answer-field/choices 17592186191001] {:db/id 17592186192792 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-629276db-5577-5de0-b4ed-4cb541d19524" "question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-629276db-5577-5de0-b4ed-4cb541d19524" :question/id #uuid "629276db-5577-5de0-b4ed-4cb541d19524" :question/math-academy-id "q-158686" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e006f41f3c8a0201623c88bd4f3738bea05258690c8a0adef297769341a3f490.png)\n\nGiven that $r$, $s$ and $t$ in the above diagram are parallel, find $m∠1.$" :question/worked-solution "Consider $∠2$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/2b/2bca55a68d4a0695c73f82ca82d5fae386d9b8d57b058bc1cf694bee902cff25.png)\n\nNotice that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${42}^{∘}$ are alternate exterior angles formed when the transversal $u$ cuts the parallel lines $r$ and $s.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠2={42}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that the angle determined by $∠1$ and $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${108}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed when the transversal $v$ cuts the parallel lines $s$ and $t.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠1+m∠2={108}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $m∠2$ into the equation, we can find $m∠1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2 & ={108}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{42}^{∘} & ={108}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={66}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f103b71a-3895-5bbb-9e5b-34cbab5a6e85"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f103b71a-3895-5bbb-9e5b-34cbab5a6e85" :answer-field/id #uuid "f103b71a-3895-5bbb-9e5b-34cbab5a6e85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c95af01a-89de-5e7a-af1b-8256384ea06b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef27bd67-7618-5a40-88e1-2590421dc7a9" "answer-c95af01a-89de-5e7a-af1b-8256384ea06b" "answer-8698773b-0f0c-5034-aa7f-9e6b850c7169" "answer-8df7c2df-5ee2-59e1-bdbf-8bf112440439" "answer-caf3290d-1f86-5c91-9631-5c5198c4c243"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef27bd67-7618-5a40-88e1-2590421dc7a9" :answer/id #uuid "ef27bd67-7618-5a40-88e1-2590421dc7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c95af01a-89de-5e7a-af1b-8256384ea06b" :answer/id #uuid "c95af01a-89de-5e7a-af1b-8256384ea06b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{66}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8698773b-0f0c-5034-aa7f-9e6b850c7169" :answer/id #uuid "8698773b-0f0c-5034-aa7f-9e6b850c7169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{68}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8df7c2df-5ee2-59e1-bdbf-8bf112440439" :answer/id #uuid "8df7c2df-5ee2-59e1-bdbf-8bf112440439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{72}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf3290d-1f86-5c91-9631-5c5198c4c243" :answer/id #uuid "caf3290d-1f86-5c91-9631-5c5198c4c243" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac" :question/id #uuid "cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-158688" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f1cb5dc40aec6a6a6402d01c50ed85d30c7992606d9957b92084a0a097823c4.png)\n\nGiven that $r$, $s$ and $t$ in the above diagram are parallel, find $m∠1.$" :question/worked-solution "Consider $∠2$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/5a/5afb2a0f9f26dc3c02b52ac50743e9541f587349267b0c322cb2644b09c48617.png)\n\nNotice that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${66}^{∘}$ are alternate exterior angles formed when the transversal $v$ cuts the parallel lines $r$ and $s.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠2={66}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that the angle determined by $∠1$ and $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${127}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed when the transversal $u$ cuts the parallel lines $s$ and $t.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠1+m∠2={127}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $m∠2$ into the equation, we can find $m∠1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2 & ={127}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{66}^{∘} & ={127}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={61}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/id #uuid "70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" "answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" "answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" "answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" "answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" :answer/id #uuid "f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{53}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" :answer/id #uuid "a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer/id #uuid "33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{61}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" :answer/id #uuid "5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{66}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74" :answer/id #uuid "d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{69}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193185 :question/problem "![](images/51/5178d7f2910b4a28116022968e6a2d5580b9284d65bb7dc973e36f4c2a2f4ccd.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{↔}{AB}∥\\overset{↔}{CF},$ what is the measure of $∠AFB?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $∠BAF$  and $∠AFC$ are alternate interior angles formed when the transversal $\\overset{↔}{AF}$ cuts the parallel lines $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ and $\\overset{↔}{CF}.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠AFC=m∠BAF={71}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/bf/bfb1ce1e2aba3efe901251ad40f84fda062e8324c4dd7a1f2888081724679842.png)\n\nAlso, notice that $∠FBE$  and $∠BFC$ are alternate interior angles formed when the transversal $\\overset{↔}{BF}$ cuts the parallel lines $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ and $\\overset{↔}{CF}.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠BFC=m∠FBE={139}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, using the angle addition postulate, we can find $∠AFB:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AFB & =m∠BFC-m∠AFC \\\\  & ={139}^{∘}-{71}^{∘} \\\\  & ={68}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186190996 :answer-field/correct "answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" "answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" "answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" "answer-1e757923-be14-5077-9aa9-a10fe8134a56" "answer-d56434a5-ddf0-597d-be37-b19db9d7ca53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" :answer/id #uuid "375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" :answer/id #uuid "823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{66}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" :an