.$"] ["question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac" :question/worked-solution "Consider $∠2$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/5a/5afb2a0f9f26dc3c02b52ac50743e9541f587349267b0c322cb2644b09c48617.png)\n\nNotice that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${66}^{∘}$ are alternate exterior angles formed when the transversal $v$ cuts the parallel lines $r$ and $s.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠2={66}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that the angle determined by $∠1$ and $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${127}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed when the transversal $u$ cuts the parallel lines $s$ and $t.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠1+m∠2={127}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $m∠2$ into the equation, we can find $m∠1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2 & ={127}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{66}^{∘} & ={127}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={61}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/id #uuid "70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd"] ["answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" :answer/id #uuid "f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df"] ["answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df" :answer/value "{53}^{∘}"] ["answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" :answer/id #uuid "a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b"] ["answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b" :answer/value "{57}^{∘}"] ["answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer/id #uuid "33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440"] ["answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440" :answer/value "{61}^{∘}"] ["answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" :answer/id #uuid "5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c"] ["answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c" :answer/value "{66}^{∘}"] ["answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74" :answer/id #uuid "d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74"] ["answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74" :answer/value "{69}^{∘}"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/correct "answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/choices "answer-f7fdc5c3-1a1e-5f72-b392-a3e4399ed4df"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/choices "answer-a353db00-3bd9-5418-b1a7-d5c0cb85203b"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/choices "answer-33302008-aa55-56c7-bf1e-e55a835f4440"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/choices "answer-5bd8f886-846d-5e11-b514-e23f590ce77c"] ["answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd" :answer-field/choices "answer-d7db8ed6-3853-5c35-a03f-c6dcacaddf74"] ["question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-70727cad-1fa5-57b5-a403-bf29c9a59dfd"] [17592186192792 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cc803095-076a-5b93-b2c7-da97793184ac"] [17592186193185 :question/problem "![](images/51/5178d7f2910b4a28116022968e6a2d5580b9284d65bb7dc973e36f4c2a2f4ccd.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{↔}{AB}∥\\overset{↔}{CF},$ what is the measure of $∠AFB?$"] [17592186193185 :question/worked-solution "Notice that $∠BAF$  and $∠AFC$ are alternate interior angles formed when the transversal $\\overset{↔}{AF}$ cuts the parallel lines $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ and $\\overset{↔}{CF}.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠AFC=m∠BAF={71}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/bf/bfb1ce1e2aba3efe901251ad40f84fda062e8324c4dd7a1f2888081724679842.png)\n\nAlso, notice that $∠FBE$  and $∠BFC$ are alternate interior angles formed when the transversal $\\overset{↔}{BF}$ cuts the parallel lines $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ and $\\overset{↔}{CF}.$ Hence, \n\n$$\nm∠BFC=m∠FBE={139}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, using the angle addition postulate, we can find $∠AFB:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AFB & =m∠BFC-m∠AFC \\\\  & ={139}^{∘}-{71}^{∘} \\\\  & ={68}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186193185 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" :answer/id #uuid "375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1"] ["answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1" :answer/value "{65}^{∘}"] ["answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" :answer/id #uuid "823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45"] ["answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45" :answer/value "{66}^{∘}"] ["answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" :answer/id #uuid "07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe"] ["answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe" :answer/value "{68}^{∘}"] ["answer-1e757923-be14-5077-9aa9-a10fe8134a56" :answer/id #uuid "1e757923-be14-5077-9aa9-a10fe8134a56"] ["answer-1e757923-be14-5077-9aa9-a10fe8134a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1e757923-be14-5077-9aa9-a10fe8134a56" :answer/value "{71}^{∘}"] ["answer-d56434a5-ddf0-597d-be37-b19db9d7ca53" :answer/id #uuid "d56434a5-ddf0-597d-be37-b19db9d7ca53"] ["answer-d56434a5-ddf0-597d-be37-b19db9d7ca53" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d56434a5-ddf0-597d-be37-b19db9d7ca53" :answer/value "{75}^{∘}"] [17592186190996 :answer-field/correct "answer-07dd7dbb-1d31-58ac-93ec-fcfc332956fe"] [17592186190996 :answer-field/choices "answer-375400ff-c52d-5bbf-907d-e17f2006ada1"] [17592186190996 :answer-field/choices "answer-823a6e7f-c033-5efb-8a44-adace0500a45"] [1759